{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1565094-my-homebrew-horror-stuff","id":1565094,"title":"My Homebrew Horror stuff","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-11-02T19:52:36-08:00","id":1565094,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> My Homebrew Horror stuff","content":"So, I've made some Homebrew Dread Powers. They're originally for Hunter but can technically be used for any gameline or Horror. Any suggestions or feedback is appreciated. <br /> <b>Undead Resistance: </b>Their body reacts to injury the same way, they just don't need things like intact organs or functioning blood vessels to keep going. Treat sources of damage that are Lethal to Mortals as Bashing except for Banes.<br /> <br /> <b>Play Dead: </b>By spending 1 Willpower, the monster can cease all signs of life as if they were dead. They cannot move while in this state.<br /> <br /> <b>Psychometry</b>: The monster can see into the past, whether with an object or person (whether they're alive or dead). They spend 1 Willpower make a fitting roll to learn the past of an object, person, or corpse they come into contact with.<br /> <br /> <b>Transformation</b>: The monster gains +3 strength, +2 stamina, +2 size, and +1 Dexterirty. The user spends 1 Willpower for every [potency] turns they remain in the transformation and once they stop spending the cost it either ends or they enter a mindless rage. (Made by a friend of mine, but I'm not sure they're active here.)<br /> <br /> <b>Spirit Partner</b>: the monster is bonded to an Ephemeral Being. By Spending WP, it may merge with it and swap out its Attributes for the Ephemeral Being's. At Storyteller Discretion, it may also gain other abilities<br /> <br /> <b>Second Sight</b>: The Horror can see beyond mortal eyes. Whenever any magical effect is activated within (Potency) *2 meters, the horror becomes aware of it. By Spending 1 WP, they roll Wits + Occult to get the answer to one of the following:<br /> <br /> 1. What's the source? (ie, Who or what is outputting the magic.) <br /> 2. What is it manipulating? (ie, a target, the environment, fate?) <br /> 3. What is its nature? (ie, demonic, fae, spiritual, bloodline, etc)<br /> <br /> <b>Bullet Time \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> The monster has a heightened ability to avoid attacks. Adds dots of this Dread Power to Defense and allows Defense to be applied to Firearms.<br /> <br /> <b>Crafter's Blessing:</b> With just a whisper and a caress, the Horror hones a tool to a state of perfection. With an appropriate roll after spending one 1 Willpower, the equipment bonus of an item is increased by the successes of the roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Sculpt \u2022 to \u2022\u2022: </b>This Power forces even the hardiest of substances to yield to the Horror\u2019s intent. By Spending a point of Willpower and making the appropriate roll, the Horror can sculpt and alter the object to their whims. With one dot, it can only be sizes 1-3, but with two, it can be sizes 4-5 or even above at Storyteller's discretion. It cannot change the size of substance, only the shape. If used on anything mechanical, it either destroys the original function or requires a Wits + Crafts roll to maintain it or give the item some sort of new function.<br /> <br /> <b>Ephemeral Sight \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> The Horror is able to perceive a Frequency of Twilight. 1 dot means only one, 2 means the most common Frequencies (Ghosts, Spirits, and Angels), and 3 means all frequencies of Twilight.<br /> <br /> <b>Shapeshift: </b>The monster can alter subtle parts of their features: Moles and scars can be added, the colors of the hair and eyes can be changed, and they can even become a different apparent race or gender. 1 Wp is spent per specific use of this power; They can use that to make whatever changes they wish, but if they wish to make a change to their disguise after they've already settled on one they must spend another WP (e.g One can choose to look like a white woman with blonde hair with one initial spending, but if they want to change to a brunette later they have to spend another WP.) becoming a different person can be challenging and thus requires a roll to successfully perform with this power.<br /> <br /> <b>Body Double:</b> the Horror replaces a person with a substitute under their control. They must render their victim unconscious and take him somewhere private \u2014 many prefer to use their personal lair if possible. The Horror uses the sleeping victim as a template, crafting a doppelganger from their preferred materials. Some use mud and clay, others grow replacement humans in giant seed pods.<br /> <br /> <b>Spoof \u2022 to \u2022\u2022:</b> Discerning information about the Horror is difficult, inflicting a Penalty equal to Potency to attempts to interrogate or manipulate them and inflicting the Confused condition on a Dramatic Failure. At two dots, they get a second Virtue or Vice and can use that to mislead attempts to guess it.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmare Form \u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022:</b> the Monster takes the guise of a particularly horrific form. Activating this power requires a point of Willpower and a reflexive action to activate. When activating this Dread Power, choose whether to make a single change, or the whole body. Each unique appliance on the body should have clearly-stated benefits. Those benefits may be equipment modifiers, armor, weapon bonuses, or other effects with the modifiers being divided amongst these benefits (+2 per dot for equipment including weapons, equal to dots for everything else.) For example, a drill hand with 2 dots might offer +2 to Crafts rolls, as well as acting like a 2 lethal weapon. A skin made of raw, exposed electrical wiring with three dots may offer 1 point of armor and cause 2 points of damage to anyone touched by the monster. As a rule, you can choose one major feature for each dot in the Dread Power. Most monsters maintain one specific form, and call on it at any time they need. Some can adapt their bodies in the moment and change each time they invoke this power. (update of Biomechanical Nightmare from Hunter: Mortal Remains.)<br /> <br /> <b>Voodoo Doll: </b>Can inflict damage on the victim through an effigy made from using a personal item of the victim's, including things like hair and blood samples, being able to inflict Bashing or Lethal Damage with a roll depending on how they damage the effigy. For other potentially more nuanced effects, the Hex Dread Power is recommended.<br /> <br /> <b>Squatters Rights: </b>The monster declares their right to be on the premises, persuading the home that it belongs there. By spending 2 Willpower, they may then bypass any mundane security systems \u2014 It does not show on cameras, for instance \u2014 and its doors automatically open for it. Animal stay out of its way.<br /> <br /> <b>Escape Artist: </b>The monster can escape restraints with ease. If bound or held, the monster can simply slip free Of the bonds \u2014 escaping a grapple, or slipping free of Manacles. To do so, she spends a Willpower as a reflexive Action. It automatically gains freedom from whatever was holding them. However, this may be circumvented by being made of the Bane of the creature involved or via a Ban.<br /> <br /> <b>Rally \u2022 to \u2022\u2022: </b>The Monster is able to boost the prowess of any allies it has, making them fight and perform harder. By spending 1 Willpower, the monster is able to give an ally a +3 bonus. They are not able to use this ability on themselves. At one dot it's for one action and two it lasts the entire scene. It only can be done once per person in a scene.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27928-supernoah9999","name":"Supernoah9999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}